# Supabase conventions (auto-applied to DB/realtime/server files)

- Every table has RLS enabled with explicit policies. New tables must ship policies
  in the same migration.
- State transitions that must be conflict-free are `security definer` functions with a
  guarded `UPDATE ... WHERE <valid-transition>` so concurrent callers can't double-apply.
- Add new realtime tables to the `supabase_realtime` publication in the migration.
- Audit every critical mutation into `audit_log` (actor + action + optional detail).
- Migrations are additive and idempotent where possible (`add column if not exists`,
  `create ... if not exists`). Never rewrite `schema.sql` in place for a change —
  add a new numbered migration (e.g. `supabase/002_add_cabins.sql`).
- Server routes that use the service role must verify a shared secret or the caller's
  session first. Never expose service-role capability to an unauthenticated path.
